{"path":"io/basic_spanbuf/setbuf","title":"std::basic_spanbuf<CharT,Traits>::setbuf","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::basic_spanbuf&lt;CharT,Traits&gt;::</span>setbuf","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/io/basic_spanbuf/setbuf","section":"io","kind":"page","summary":"Makes the basic_spanbuf perform I/O on the buffer [s, s + n). Equivalently calls this->span(std::span<CharT>(s, n)) and then returns this.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx23\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">protected</span><span class=\"sy4\">:</span><br><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_streambuf\"><span class=\"kw1683\">std::<span class=\"me2\">basic_streambuf</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>CharT, Traits<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy2\">*</span> setbuf<span class=\"br0\">(</span> CharT <span class=\"sy2\">*</span>s, <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/streamsize\"><span class=\"kw1821\">std::<span class=\"me2\">streamsize</span></span></a> n <span class=\"br0\">)</span> override<span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx23\">(since C++23)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Makes the <code>basic_spanbuf</code> perform I/O on the buffer <span><code>[</code><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">s</span></code><code>,&nbsp;</code><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">s <span class=\"sy2\">+</span> n</span></code><code>)</code></span>. Equivalently calls <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">this<span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span>span<span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/container/span\"><span class=\"kw2648\">std::<span class=\"me2\">span</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>CharT<span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>s, n<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> and then returns <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">this</span></code>.\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\">\n<tr>\n<th rowspan=\"2\">Set bits in open mode<br>(affecting pointers to get area)\n</th>\n<th colspan=\"3\">Return value after setting\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_streambuf/gptr\">eback()</a></span>\n</td>\n<td><span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_streambuf/gptr\">gptr()</a></span>\n</td>\n<td><span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_streambuf/gptr\">egptr()</a></span>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/ios_base/openmode\"><span class=\"kw1691\">std::<span class=\"me2\">ios_base</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">in</span></span></a></span></code>\n</td>\n<td><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">s</span></code>\n</td>\n<td><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">s</span></code>\n</td>\n<td><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">s <span class=\"sy2\">+</span> n</span></code>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"4\">\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<th rowspan=\"2\">Set bits in open mode<br>(affecting pointers to put area)\n</th>\n<th colspan=\"3\">Return value after setting\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_streambuf/pptr\">pbase()</a></span>\n</td>\n<td><span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_streambuf/pptr\">pptr()</a></span>\n</td>\n<td><span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_streambuf/pptr\">epptr()</a></span>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/ios_base/openmode\"><span class=\"kw1692\">std::<span class=\"me2\">ios_base</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">out</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span> <span class=\"sy3\">!</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/ios_base/openmode\"><span class=\"kw1694\">std::<span class=\"me2\">ios_base</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">ate</span></span></a></span></code>\n</td>\n<td><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">s</span></code>\n</td>\n<td><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">s</span></code>\n</td>\n<td><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">s <span class=\"sy2\">+</span> n</span></code>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/ios_base/openmode\"><span class=\"kw1692\">std::<span class=\"me2\">ios_base</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">out</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy3\">&amp;&amp;</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/ios_base/openmode\"><span class=\"kw1694\">std::<span class=\"me2\">ios_base</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">ate</span></span></a></span></code>\n</td>\n<td><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">s</span></code>\n</td>\n<td><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">s <span class=\"sy2\">+</span> n</span></code>\n</td>\n<td><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">s <span class=\"sy2\">+</span> n</span></code>\n</td></tr></table>\n<p>This function is protected virtual, it may only be called through <code>pubsetbuf()</code> or from member functions of a user-defined class derived from <span class=\"t-lc\">std::basic_spanbuf</span>.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> s\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> pointer to the first <code>CharT</code> in the user-provided buffer\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> n\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> the number of <code>CharT</code> elements in the user-provided buffer\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">this</span></code>\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>The deprecated stream buffer <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/strstreambuf\">std::strstreambuf</a></span> or the boost.IOStreams device <a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.boost.org/doc/libs/release/libs/iostreams/doc/classes/array.html#array\" data-external=\"1\"><code>boost::basic_array</code></a> can also implement I/O buffering over a user-provided <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">char</span></span></code> array.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-notice\">This section is incomplete<br>Reason: no example </div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_streambuf/pubsetbuf\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>pubsetbuf</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  invokes <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">setbuf<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code> <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function of <code>std::basic_streambuf&lt;CharT,Traits&gt;</code>)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/basic_stringbuf/setbuf\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>setbuf</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-cmark\">[virtual]</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  attempts to replace the controlled character sequence with an array <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(virtual protected member function of <code>std::basic_stringbuf&lt;CharT,Traits,Allocator&gt;</code>)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/strstreambuf/setbuf\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>setbuf</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-cmark\">[virtual]</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  attempts to replace the controlled character sequence with an array <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(virtual protected member function of <code>std::strstreambuf</code>)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"io","title":"Input/output library"},{"path":"io/basic_spanbuf","title":"std::basic_spanbuf"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::basic_spanbuf<CharT,Traits>::setbuf","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration; revisions: since C++23. Makes the basic_spanbuf perform I/O on the buffer [s, s + n)."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"s, n"},{"label":"Return value","note":"this"},{"label":"Notes","note":"The deprecated stream buffer std::strstreambuf or the boost.IOStreams device boost::basic_array can also implement I/O buffering over a user-provided char…"},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"pubsetbuf","note":"invokes setbuf()"},{"label":"setbuf","note":"attempts to replace the controlled character sequence with an array"},{"label":"setbuf","note":"attempts to replace the controlled character sequence with an array"}]}]},"standards":["C++23"],"wordCount":208,"codeBlockCount":0}
